What is streams?
Collection stores the data, stream process the data
A stream is a sequence of elements that allows you to process data in a clean an functional way

Collections->stream() -> intermediate operations -> terminal operations -> result

Intermediate operations:

Intermediate operations transform stream into another stream

filter(), map(), sorted(), distinct(), limit(), skip(),flatMap(),

They are lazy, meaning they dont actually process the data until a terminal operational is called

Terminal Operations:

terminal operations finish the stream pipelings

forEach(), collect(), count(), reduce() , findFirst(), findAny(), anyMatch(),allMatch(),
noneMatch(),min(),max(),

Combining operations



